  "description": "The Gold Coast, Australia network from Veitch Lister Consultancy, provided by M. Bliemer and converted by D. Rey, as revised in January 2016; its links carry critical speed and lane count columns in place of toll and link type. From Transportation Networks for Research, the traffic assignment test networks that continue H. Bar-Gera's TNTP collection, read from the repository at commit d1639b4ef218 in the TNTP format: the network file's links are directed edges of type link carrying capacity, length, freeFlowTime, b, power, speed, criticalSpeed, lanes, and nodes 1 to 1068 are zones (type zone) and the rest of type node; each origin-destination entry of the trip table is a node of type commodity carrying its demand, joined by an origin edge and a destination edge to its two zones, zero entries included as the file lists them. The node coordinate files are not read.",
